<title>TURKMENISTAN: Turkmen '96 nat gas output up 9.0 pct to 35.2 bcm.</title>
<headline>Turkmen '96 nat gas output up 9.0 pct to 35.2 bcm.</headline>
<dateline>ASHGABAT 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkmenistan's production of natural gas rose nine percent in 1996 to 35.18 billion cubic metres (bcm) from the year before, a report from the State Statistics Committee said on Thursday.</p>
<p>It gave no absolute comparative figures.</p>
<p> TURKMEN ENERGY OUTPUT	 Dec 96     Nov 96    Jan-Dec 96</p>
<p>Natural gas</p>
<p> (billion cubic metres)	 2.766	2.669     35.182</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct change	   +3.7	 -0.7	  n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr   pct change	    n/a	  n/a	 +9.0</p>
<p> Crude oil (mln tonnes)	 0.34	 0.36	 4.025</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct change	   -4.9	 -3.6	  n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr   pct change	    n/a	  n/a	 +6.6</p>
<p> Gasoline (tonnes)	     61,200     51,600    718,400</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct change	  +18.6	 -7.4	  n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr   pct change	    n/a	  n/a	+17.3</p>
<p> Diesel (mln tonnes)	    0.10	 0.16	 1.47</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct change	  -36.5	+53.3	  n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr   pct change	    n/a	  n/a	 +7.1</p>
<p> Fuel oil (mazut) (mln tonnes)0.10	 0.11	 1.50</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct change	   -9.0	 +2.2	  n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr  pct change	     n/a	  n/a	+10.1</p>
<p>-- Almaty Newsroom +7 3272 509410</p>
</text>
